---
// Backup and recovery: which loss the phrase covers, and which it does not.
---

<svg
  class="u-dg"
  viewBox="0 0 640 556"
  role="img"
  aria-labelledby="dg-rec-t dg-rec-d"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
>
  <title id="dg-rec-t">Which loss the recovery phrase covers, and the one it does not</title>
  <desc id="dg-rec-d">
    The recovery phrase is drawn as the root of everything. From it are derived
    every account, on every network, in every address type, on any device and in
    any compatible wallet. Settings are drawn separately and outside it: connected
    sites, address labels, contacts, frozen coins and spending limits live on the
    device only and are not carried by the phrase. Five situations are then mapped
    to outcomes. Forgetting the password is recoverable: the password unlocks one
    installation and is not the backup, so you reinstall and restore from the
    phrase. Losing or breaking the device is recoverable the same way. Deleting the
    extension is recoverable the same way. Having someone see the phrase is not a
    loss of access but a loss of secrecy: the funds must be moved to a wallet made
    from a new phrase, because the old phrase cannot be made secret again. Losing
    the phrase while still able to unlock the wallet is urgent but survivable:
    reveal and write down the phrase now, or move the funds to a wallet you do
    have the phrase for. Losing the phrase while locked out is the one case with no
    recovery path at all, by anyone, including Universe.
  </desc>

  <text class="dg-kicker" x="0" y="14">WHAT THE PHRASE COVERS</text>

  <!-- Root -->
  <rect class="dg-panel-2" x="0.75" y="26.75" width="310.5" height="150.5" rx="4" />
  <text class="dg-h" x="16" y="50">The phrase carries</text>
  <path class="dg-rule" d="M16 62 L296 62" />
  <text class="dg-sm" x="16" y="86">Every account in the wallet</text>
  <text class="dg-sm" x="16" y="110">Every network</text>
  <text class="dg-sm" x="16" y="134">Every address type</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="16" y="162">On any device, in any BIP-39 wallet</text>

  <rect class="dg-panel" x="328.75" y="26.75" width="310.5" height="150.5" rx="4" />
  <text class="dg-h" x="344" y="50">The phrase does not carry</text>
  <path class="dg-rule" d="M344 62 L624 62" />
  <text class="dg-sm" x="344" y="86">Connected sites, labels, contacts</text>
  <text class="dg-sm" x="344" y="110">Frozen coins and spending limits</text>
  <text class="dg-sm" x="344" y="134">Your password</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="344" y="162">These are device settings, not funds</text>

  <text class="dg-kicker" x="0" y="212">WHICH LOSS YOU ARE HAVING</text>

  <!-- Cases -->
  <rect class="dg-panel" x="0.75" y="224.75" width="638.5" height="52.5" rx="3" />
  <text class="dg-sm" x="16" y="248">You forgot the password</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="16" y="268">The password unlocks one installation. It is not the backup.</text>
  <path class="dg-rule" d="M356 234 L356 268" />
  <text class="dg-sm" x="372" y="256">Reinstall, then restore from the phrase.</text>

  <rect class="dg-panel" x="0.75" y="286.75" width="638.5" height="52.5" rx="3" />
  <text class="dg-sm" x="16" y="310">The device is lost, stolen or broken</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="16" y="330">Your coins were never on the device. They are on the chain.</text>
  <path class="dg-rule" d="M356 296 L356 330" />
  <text class="dg-sm" x="372" y="318">Restore from the phrase, elsewhere.</text>

  <rect class="dg-panel" x="0.75" y="348.75" width="638.5" height="52.5" rx="3" />
  <text class="dg-sm" x="16" y="372">The extension was removed</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="16" y="392">Reinstalling gives you an empty wallet, not your wallet.</text>
  <path class="dg-rule" d="M356 358 L356 392" />
  <text class="dg-sm" x="372" y="380">Restore from the phrase.</text>

  <rect class="dg-alert-panel" x="0.75" y="410.75" width="638.5" height="52.5" rx="3" />
  <text class="dg-sm" x="16" y="434">Someone else has seen the phrase</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="16" y="454">A phrase cannot be made secret again.</text>
  <path class="dg-rule" d="M356 420 L356 454" />
  <text class="dg-sm dg-alert-text" x="372" y="442">Move everything to a new phrase now.</text>

  <rect class="dg-alert-panel" x="0.75" y="472.75" width="638.5" height="82.5" rx="3" />
  <text class="dg-sm" x="16" y="496">The phrase is gone and you are locked out</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="16" y="516">There is no account, no reset email, and no</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="16" y="536">support override that can help here.</text>
  <path class="dg-rule" d="M356 482 L356 544" />
  <text class="dg-sm dg-alert-text" x="372" y="506">No recovery path exists.</text>
  <text class="dg-sm" x="372" y="528">Anyone who says otherwise is</text>
  <text class="dg-sm" x="372" y="546">selling you a second theft.</text>
</svg>
